      "side": 1,
      "message": "This (the fact that I need to add a flag to `SkDeserialProcs`) is the part of this CL that I really dislike. Having the flag on `SkReadBuffer` seems fairly clean, as is the error-checking in the various `CreateProc` factories. The problem is that we need to propagate the flag into the new `SkReadBuffer` that\u0027s created when we deserialize this picture, and there\u0027s no good way to communicate that down. We have to hop through several levels:\n```\nSkPicture::MakeFromData\nSkPicture::MakeFromStreamPriv\nSkPictureData::CreateFromStream\nSkPictureData::parseStream\nSkPictureData::parseStreamTag\n```\n\nThe `SkDeserialProcs` are already plumbed through that whole chain (and also propagate to nested pictures), but it\u0027s a public structure, and everthing else here is private. (Also, it\u0027s not even a proc, just a flag).",
      "revId": "076b8aace4edbd5c9cfc25dbdf4f2d8b07a0d01f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
