      "message": "It is a proc, you just have to pick between two implementations, one that always returns true and one that always returns false. Given that this proc takes no parameters and returns bool, that seems fairly logical. If it did take a parameter then it might make more sense to allow picking between more implementations (allow someone to write their own). Would be interesting to try to implement this as an enum with function pointer underlying type (I know, can\u0027t be expressed in the language, but that\u0027s what is being done here).",
